    <meta property="og:description" content="Microcystins are cyanobacterial toxins that remain a global threat to freshwater health and function despite decades of study. This Review summarizes controls of toxin production, persistence and degradation on scales from genes to ecosystems, as well as current management strategies, constructed wetlands as nature-based solutions, and future research priorities."/>
